    "code":  "VIRAL_HEPATITIS_B",
    "name":  "Viral hepatitis B",
    "module":  "hepatobiliary",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Hepatitis B is a viral infection caused by the hepatitis B virus (HBV), transmitted through blood, sexual contact, and vertical (mother-to-child) transmission. Acute HBV causes a self-limiting illness with jaundice, fatigue, right upper quadrant pain, and elevated transaminases in most adults; fewer than 1% develop acute liver failure. Chronic HBV (defined as HBsAg positivity \u003e6 months) develops in 90% of perinatally infected neonates and 5–10% of immunocompetent adults. Chronic infection carries significant risk of cirrhosis and hepatocellular carcinoma. Effective vaccines and antiviral therapy (tenofovir, entecavir) are available.",
